# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00179 Task 0.7: deploys stt-watch.timer, which runs stt over stt_watch_folders every
# 5 minutes, and its failure notification. Set stt_watch_folders in host_vars first.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml

# Plan 00194 Task 2.0b: the host's pingbus kit (seat disconnected) for the ccy launcher's exit,
# and the member kit's settings with the longer SessionEnd bound. Before play-claude-yolo.yml.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml

# CCY 3.99.12.11: deploys the launcher whose compose start question is asked once per launch,
# a no kept (it used to be asked again straight after). The image is unchanged: no rebuild.
# Plan 00204 D4 and Plan 00201 Task 2.17: rebuilds ccy-teams and ccy-sessions, nothing to
# restart; running sessions are not touched. Every screen has a context heading saying where it
# is and what it acts on (Teams › alpha › Add LXC member · step 3/4 Checkout over "into team
# alpha · container …"; ccy --teams heads each team "New session › Team 2 of 3: …"; Teams ›
# <team> › Settings), wrapped at its › and · separators on a narrow terminal, never cut off.
# Every seat is shown by its whole handle (<repo>.<seat>+<host>.<type>, the coordinator's with
# (coordinator) beside it) in the list, --list, the menus and the headings; the table's columns
# are sized to their longest value and nothing is cut short, and on a narrow terminal TEAM,
# MEMBER, KIND and STATE stay on the row and the rest shows above the headings. ccy-teams and
# ccy-sessions no longer offer a host or podman session in a checkout inside an LXC container's
# files (read from /etc/lxc/lxc.conf, no root needed); they point to ccy-teams lxc-add instead.
# Plan 00194 Task 2.0b: ccy 3.99.12.14, container 2.77.10, so the image IS rebuilt on the next
# launch: the goodbye is no longer cut off when a session ends with Ctrl-C, and a session ended
# without it (podman stop, a closed terminal, a crash) is told "disconnected" by the launcher,
# which a closed terminal or a mashed Ctrl-C no longer stops.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
